Z||000000||Predator||10-20-2000||10:31 AM||||Hey,<BR> Anybody know the guy Roman that runs the Georgia Fiero club? I was told he was the head of it, so I have been sending him emails inquiring about joining, but I cannot get any responce from him. I thought it <BR>would be fun to be part of a Fiero club since I love mine so much. I am getting the Design One Turbo kit for it today  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif">||||reg||5
Z||000001||Raydar||10-20-2000||10:48 AM||||The Ga. Fieros is still headed by Ramon Otero. He's pretty busy lately. Sometimes I think his mail falls off the server before it gets read.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> <BR>We generally meet at the American Pie on Roswell Rd (just outside 285), on the last Saturday of each month, unless there is an event going on. Due to personal time constraints, Ramon sometimes doesn't make all the meetings, but many of us are there <I>every</I> time. Come on out!  <P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
Z||000002||1FST2M6||10-20-2000||01:58 PM||||All the Ga. Fiero Club members are great people and Ramon, and Steve (Raydar) are a wealth of knowlege! Lunch usually lasts 45 min then you spend 3 hours in the parking lot talking or takings others for a slide or two around the block..    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/smile.gif"> right steve!    <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"> i've tainted a few members with the nitrous bug!  NITROUS IS COOL!  humm.. nitrous and a big snail.. hummmm  i won't be to a meeting till january... NOT going till my car is DONE! <P>oh another forum member msweldon (Marc) will probly be joining soon as well.. Hey steve.. why isn't Don or Ramon on here?!? Don still computerless? <P>WOW  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif"> i've got over 1000 posts! <BR>------------------<BR>Shhh.. Top Secret! <BR>   <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/1fstcheeto_2.jpg">   <p>[This message has been edited by 1FST2M6 (edited 10-20-2000).]||||reg||1
Z||000003||msweldon||10-20-2000||02:27 PM||||Waddup Predator,<P>Computers and Fieros, sounds like my long lost brother.<P>I've had a fiero for 11years and just found this forum and other fiero enthusiasts for the first time.<P>I'll probably be joining 1FST2M6 in January at the meeting,(never thought orange would look so good on a car) I'm in the midst of planning a DOHC swap so maybe I'll have it done by then, maybe not...<P>have fun,<BR>marc<P>Keep us posted on the design one kit.||||reg||1
Z||000004||Raydar||10-20-2000||02:53 PM||||Travis, <P>Wealth of knowledge? Me?!? I just <I>talk</I> a lot.<BR>I'm still bugging Don to get online. Told him I'd set him up, turn-key, if he ever got ready. Showed him the Forum. He seems to be real intimidated by computers, though.<BR>Ramon is waaayyyy too busy to hang out on here. He's been marrying off his kids at an alarming rate.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/eek.gif">  J/K!!! <BR>Ramon was asking for ya'. Said to tell you to come to the meetings and not to be a stranger.<BR>Speaking of alarming...<BR>I still wanna know what you're gonna do with that snail thing. Thought you were gonna do a V-8.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/wink.gif"><P>Marc and Predator... come on out when ya' can. We'll be lookin' for ya'.<P>------------------<BR>Raydar<P>Out of my mind.<BR>Back in five minutes.||||reg||1
